1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,937
<i>Coco (thinking): Don't let Tiko find out!</i>

2
00:00:02,587 --> 00:00:04,509
<i>Professor Shellby (thinking): He must never know...</i>

3
00:00:04,209 --> 00:00:06,151
<i>Sparky (thinking): Tonight... everything changes.</i>

4
00:00:06,199 --> 00:00:08,371
Wait... I can hear what everyone is THINKING?!

5
00:00:14,502 --> 00:00:18,234
<i>Narrator: One morning, in Fernwood Valley... a few hours earlier.</i>

6
00:00:18,696 --> 00:00:22,061
Tiko! Tiko! Watch this! My biggest fireball ever!

7
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:25,060
Last time you did that, you sneezed on my head.

8
00:00:25,688 --> 00:00:26,785
That was one time!

9
00:00:27,413 --> 00:00:28,900
It was four times. Today.

10
00:00:29,844 --> 00:00:31,397
Ah... ah... CHOO!

11
00:00:35,044 --> 00:00:35,944
Whoa!

12
00:00:35,344 --> 00:00:36,244
Yikes!

13
00:00:36,494 --> 00:00:38,097
...Did I just shoot down a star?

14
00:00:38,725 --> 00:00:39,956
You shot down a STAR!

15
00:00:42,902 --> 00:00:44,553
Whoa... it's warm. And it's humming.

16
00:00:45,181 --> 00:00:47,788
Don't touch it! What if it's a sneeze star?

17
00:00:47,588 --> 00:00:50,475
What if it's MY sneeze, coming back for revenge?

18
00:00:52,353 --> 00:00:53,253
Ah!

19
00:00:54,103 --> 00:00:57,115
Ow... my ears are buzzing. Sparky, did you say something?

20
00:00:57,743 --> 00:01:00,448
Nope. I'm totally fine. Not hungry at all.

21
00:01:01,076 --> 00:01:04,077
<i>Sparky (thinking): I'm SO hungry. I could eat a whole tree. With the bark.</i>

22
00:01:04,705 --> 00:01:05,631
...You're hungry.

23
00:01:06,259 --> 00:01:07,371
How did you know that?

24
00:01:07,999 --> 00:01:09,568
You just said it. "With the bark."

25
00:01:10,196 --> 00:01:11,549
I did NOT say that out loud!

26
00:01:12,177 --> 00:01:14,108
Okay... think of a number. Any number.

27
00:01:14,736 --> 00:01:17,226
<i>Sparky (thinking): Seven. No, too easy. Eleventy-twelve!</i>

28
00:01:17,854 --> 00:01:19,542
Eleventy-twelve isn't a number.

29
00:01:20,170 --> 00:01:23,431
AAAH! You're inside my head! Get out! It's messy in there!

30
00:01:24,059 --> 00:01:26,795
Sparky... I think this star lets me read minds.

31
00:01:27,423 --> 00:01:31,122
That's the coolest thing that has ever happened. And also the scariest.

32
00:01:31,750 --> 00:01:33,782
Come on! Let's test it on somebody else!

33
00:01:38,716 --> 00:01:43,355
Ah. Good morning, young ones. Lovely day... for a slow walk.

34
00:01:43,983 --> 00:01:49,438
<i>Professor Shellby (thinking): Now where on earth did I put my glasses? I've been looking since breakfast.</i>

35
00:01:50,066 --> 00:01:53,188
Good morning, Professor. Your glasses are on top of your head.

36
00:01:55,116 --> 00:01:59,443
Hm? Well, I'll be. How did you know I was looking for them?

37
00:02:00,071 --> 00:02:02,639
He reads minds now! I shot down a star!

38
00:02:03,267 --> 00:02:07,040
A star? Let me see that... Oh, my. A Thinking Star.

39
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:09,983
I read about these when I was only ninety.

40
00:02:10,611 --> 00:02:12,431
Can you read minds too, Professor?

41
00:02:13,059 --> 00:02:17,528
At my age, little dragon, I can barely read a menu.

42
00:02:18,488 --> 00:02:20,552
So it's real? I can really hear thoughts?

43
00:02:21,180 --> 00:02:26,234
Every thought, little one. But remember: a thought is like a cloud.

44
00:02:26,034 --> 00:02:30,798
It drifts by, and you only ever see one small piece of the sky.

45
00:02:31,592 --> 00:02:35,952
<i>Professor Shellby (thinking): Oh no. If he can hear thoughts... he'll find out about tonight!</i>

46
00:02:36,580 --> 00:02:38,035
Find out about what tonight?

47
00:02:38,663 --> 00:02:43,391
Hm? Nothing! Nothing at all. Oh look, a dragonfly!

48
00:02:44,019 --> 00:02:49,081
<i>Professor Shellby (thinking): Think about turnips. Think about turnips. Turnips, turnips, turnips...</i>

49
00:02:49,709 --> 00:02:52,380
He's thinking about turnips. Really, really hard.

50
00:02:53,008 --> 00:02:56,284
That's suspicious. Nobody thinks about turnips that hard.

51
00:02:56,912 --> 00:03:00,705
Tiko, darling! Sparky, sweetie! Fabulous morning, isn't it? Gorgeous!

52
00:03:00,505 --> 00:03:01,538
Simply gorgeous!

53
00:03:02,166 --> 00:03:05,384
<i>Coco (thinking): Act normal, Coco. Act normal. Don't mention the big secret.</i>

54
00:03:05,184 --> 00:03:06,868
<i>Coco (thinking): And don't look at the bushes.</i>

55
00:03:07,496 --> 00:03:09,104
Coco... what's in the bushes?

56
00:03:09,732 --> 00:03:13,237
Bushes? What bushes? I have never seen a bush in my entire life!

57
00:03:13,865 --> 00:03:15,281
You literally live in a bush.

58
00:03:15,909 --> 00:03:18,772
That is a TREE, sweetie. A very exclusive tree.

59
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:23,265
<i>Coco (thinking): Poor little Tiko. After tonight, nothing will ever be the same for him.</i>

60
00:03:23,893 --> 00:03:25,401
...Nothing will ever be the same?

61
00:03:26,029 --> 00:03:28,287
Gotta fly! Busy, busy! Toodle-oo!

62
00:03:30,252 --> 00:03:32,854
Okay. That was weird. Even for Coco.

63
00:03:33,648 --> 00:03:35,718
<i>Frog (thinking): Did anybody see me trip over that log?</i>

64
00:03:34,918 --> 00:03:37,497
<i>Bunny (thinking): I hope it doesn't rain. My ears frizz when it rains.</i>

65
00:03:36,797 --> 00:03:39,663
<i>Snail (thinking): Is that... my tail... or a snake?</i>

66
00:03:38,763 --> 00:03:41,920
<i>Beetle (thinking): Left, right, left, right... wait, which ones are my left legs?</i>

67
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:43,826
<i>Mole (thinking): Too bright. Too bright! Who turned on the sun?</i>

68
00:03:43,791 --> 00:03:46,712
Too many voices! Everybody's thinking at the same time!

69
00:03:47,340 --> 00:03:52,186
Just think about something quiet. Like clouds. Or naps. Naps are very quiet.

70
00:03:52,814 --> 00:03:56,270
There you are, my little explorer! Did you have a nice morning?

71
00:03:56,898 --> 00:03:58,706
Mama... is something happening tonight?

72
00:03:59,334 --> 00:04:03,004
Tonight? Oh, just a quiet evening. Why do you ask, sweetheart?

73
00:04:03,632 --> 00:04:08,155
<i>Mama (thinking): He's growing up so fast. It's time for him to move out of the little nest.</i>

74
00:04:07,955 --> 00:04:10,083
<i>Mama (thinking): Tonight, he leaves it... forever.</i>

75
00:04:12,974 --> 00:04:14,138
...Okay, Mama.

76
00:04:14,766 --> 00:04:19,641
Now, why don't you two go and play far away until sunset? Very far away.

77
00:04:19,441 --> 00:04:20,875
Really, really far.

78
00:04:21,503 --> 00:04:23,990
<i>Mama (thinking): And please, please, do not come back early...</i>

79
00:04:27,765 --> 00:04:30,003
Sparky... I think everyone wants me to leave.

80
00:04:30,631 --> 00:04:32,543
What? No way! Who told you that?

81
00:04:33,171 --> 00:04:36,897
Nobody TOLD me. They THOUGHT it. Mama wants me out of the nest.

82
00:04:36,697 --> 00:04:41,040
Coco says nothing will be the same. And the Professor is hiding something.

83
00:04:41,668 --> 00:04:43,414
Tiko, I'm sure there's a good—

84
00:04:43,164 --> 00:04:47,781
<i>Sparky (thinking): Don't think about the surprise! Don't think about the surprise! Bananas!</i>

85
00:04:47,581 --> 00:04:49,376
<i>Sparky (thinking): Bananas, bananas, bananas!</i>

86
00:04:50,005 --> 00:04:51,768
...Why are you thinking about bananas?

87
00:04:52,396 --> 00:04:56,515
I'm not! I'm thinking about... regular things. Normal dragon things.

88
00:04:57,143 --> 00:05:01,091
<i>Sparky (thinking): Oh no, oh no, oh no. I wish he would just go away for a while!</i>

89
00:05:03,222 --> 00:05:04,428
You too, Sparky?

90
00:05:04,477 --> 00:05:06,502
Wait, Tiko, that's not what I—

91
00:05:07,902 --> 00:05:10,968
Tiko! Come back! Oh no... I have to tell the others!

92
00:05:12,755 --> 00:05:16,681
Code red! Code red! Tiko heard everything and he ran away!

93
00:05:17,309 --> 00:05:19,554
Everything?! Even the part about the cake?

94
00:05:20,182 --> 00:05:22,672
No! Worse! He thinks we all want him to leave!

95
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:25,065
Oh no. My poor baby...

96
00:05:25,858 --> 00:05:30,126
Leave it to me. I know exactly where he goes when he is sad.

97
00:05:29,926 --> 00:05:32,635
I have known since before he hatched.

98
00:05:33,263 --> 00:05:34,523
Hurry, Professor!

99
00:05:35,151 --> 00:05:39,015
Hurrying... is not my specialty. But I shall try.

100
00:05:46,267 --> 00:05:50,153
A thought is just one piece of the sky... But what if that piece is true?

101
00:05:55,146 --> 00:05:56,843
<i>Coco (thinking): Don't let him find out!</i>

102
00:05:56,243 --> 00:05:57,360
<i>Sparky (thinking): Go away for a while!</i>

103
00:05:56,760 --> 00:05:58,095
<i>Mama (thinking): He leaves it forever!</i>

104
00:05:57,495 --> 00:05:59,185
<i>Professor Shellby (thinking): Turnips! Turnips!</i>

105
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:01,474
Stop! Stop it! I don't want to hear anymore!

106
00:06:04,364 --> 00:06:07,737
There you are. I came as fast as I could.

107
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:11,594
Which, admittedly, took about three hours.

108
00:06:12,388 --> 00:06:14,345
Professor... everyone wants me gone.

109
00:06:14,973 --> 00:06:21,060
A Thinking Star only shows you the thoughts, Tiko. Never the reasons behind them.

110
00:06:21,688 --> 00:06:28,191
In two hundred years, I've learned this: when we only hear a little, we imagine the rest.

111
00:06:27,991 --> 00:06:30,528
And we usually imagine the worst.

112
00:06:31,322 --> 00:06:33,417
So... I only heard one piece of the sky?

113
00:06:34,045 --> 00:06:39,619
So stop listening with the star... and come look with your own eyes. Follow me.

114
00:06:43,063 --> 00:06:44,831
Hello? Mama? Why is it so dark?

115
00:06:46,776 --> 00:06:48,170
SURPRISE!

116
00:06:49,170 --> 00:06:53,211
Happy Hatch Day, Tiko darling! One whole year since you popped out of your egg!

117
00:06:53,839 --> 00:06:55,016
My... hatch day?

118
00:06:55,644 --> 00:06:57,946
And that's not all. Look up, sweetheart.

119
00:07:01,843 --> 00:07:06,620
Your very own big-kid nest. Right next to mine. You're leaving the little nest...

120
00:07:06,420 --> 00:07:08,202
but you're never leaving me.

121
00:07:08,830 --> 00:07:10,001
So THAT's what you meant...

122
00:07:10,629 --> 00:07:14,834
"Nothing will ever be the same," darling, because now you are officially a big kid!

123
00:07:15,462 --> 00:07:21,411
And I am a terrible secret keeper, so I tried not to think about the party at all.

124
00:07:21,211 --> 00:07:22,883
Hence... the turnips.

125
00:07:23,511 --> 00:07:27,007
And I needed you to go away for a while so I could practice THIS!

126
00:07:32,035 --> 00:07:34,465
Ta-da! And I didn't sneeze even once!

127
00:07:35,093 --> 00:07:36,861
Sparky... I'm sorry I ran away.

128
00:07:36,661 --> 00:07:39,743
I heard your thoughts, but I didn't listen to your heart.

129
00:07:40,371 --> 00:07:44,180
That's okay. You're my best friend. Even when you're inside my head.

130
00:07:45,140 --> 00:07:49,152
I don't need this anymore. Thoughts are better when friends share them on their own.

131
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:53,433
Ah... ah... CHOO!

132
00:07:58,180 --> 00:08:01,202
Ooooh. Oh, my. Oh, darlings... I can hear EVERYTHING.

133
00:08:01,830 --> 00:08:02,914
Uh-oh.

134
00:08:03,542 --> 00:08:06,691
Professor! You think my singing sounds like a squeaky door?!

135
00:08:07,319 --> 00:08:08,510
...Turnips.

136
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:10,907
(laughing)

137
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:10,940
(laughing)

138
00:08:10,050 --> 00:08:11,652
(laughing)

139
00:08:10,150 --> 00:08:11,248
(laughing)

140
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:12,190
(laughing)

141
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:15,614
And you? I don't need a star to know what you're thinking right now...

142
00:08:16,242 --> 00:08:18,009
"I want to see the next episode!"

143
00:08:18,637 --> 00:08:23,703
<i>Narrator: Next time, on Tiko and Sparky: What if you could shrink to the size of an ant?</i>
